{"uid":"4762e3b9ea18d238","name":"test_unpause_hits_resume_endpoint","fullName":"tests.test_cli_resume#test_unpause_hits_resume_endpoint","historyId":"515724c95cb8b57efa9012a1b6badd77","time":{"start":1791946106182,"stop":1791946107625,"duration":1443},"description":"The rename (old `resume` -> `unpause`) must still hit the engine's\n    `POST /resume` (not a no-op / not renamed to a nonexistent route):\n    the response body's `resumed: true` only comes from that handler.\n\n    cure-01-02 (v0.24 B.3/operator ruling 3, #169): this used to park on\n    plain budget exhaustion (now `timed_out`) to get to a settled state\n    cheaply, but a hold now exits the engine process outright (no more\n    idling under `on_complete: idle`) -- so hitting a dead process's API\n    would just be a connection-refused error, not a `/resume` regression.\n    `/resume` unpauses a *pause*, so the natural, still-alive state to\n    prove it against is a live, non-terminal engine: in v0.36 an unreadable\n    review verdict (`STUB_REVIEW_MALFORMED_COUNT`) is an infra fault the\n    engine waits out with its API up (the engine never pauses itself).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The rename (old <code>resume</code> -&gt; <code>unpause</code>) must still hit the engine's<br />\n<code>POST /resume</code> (not a no-op / not renamed to a nonexistent route):<br />\nthe response body's <code>resumed: true</code> only comes from that handler.</p>\n<pre><code>cure-01-02 (v0.24 B.3/operator ruling 3, #169): this used to park on\nplain budget exhaustion (now `timed_out`) to get to a settled state\ncheaply, but a hold now exits the engine process outright (no more\nidling under `on_complete: idle`) -- so hitting a dead process's API\nwould just be a connection-refused error, not a `/resume` regression.\n`/resume` unpauses a *pause*, so the natural, still-alive state to\nprove it against is a live, non-terminal engine: in v0.36 an unreadable\nreview verdict (`STUB_REVIEW_MALFORMED_COUNT`) is an infra fau